0..72 Comment "// The empty type and the apartness rule. `Empty` is a data type with no"
73..148 Comment "// constructor, so a match on it has no arm and answers whatever type it is"
149..227 Comment "// asked for: `A -> Empty` is how \"not A\" is spelled. A path between two terms"
228..304 Comment "// of a data type is eliminated the same way when the terms are apart: their"
305..382 Comment "// type\'s rules converge, and their normal forms first differ at two distinct"
383..458 Comment "// constructors, so no path joins them and a match on one has no arm either"
459..519 Comment "// (Coquand, _Pattern matching with dependent types_, 1992)."
520..522 Comment "//"
523..566 Comment "// - see: #534 — `viaLambda`, `viaStated`"
567..613 Comment "// - see: #1944 — `viaBare`, `viaBareStated`"
614..668 Comment "// - see: #1948 — `viaArgument`, `viaArgumentStated`"
670..696 Comment "// The presented integers."
